## Why This Is Asked
This question checks practical, beginner-friendly steps to enforce strict per-tenant isolation in a real API stack, not just high-level definitions.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation
- JWT tenant_id verification
- PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (RLS)
- Deny-by-default authorization
- Per-endpoint guardrails and logging
- CI/CD testing for multi-tenant access

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js middleware example
function tenantMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const tokenTid = req.user?.tenant_id;
  const pathTid = req.params.tenant_id || req.body.tenant_id;
  if (!pathTid || tokenTid !== pathTid) return res.status(403).send("Forbidden");
  next();
}
```

